  "reason": "We have a multimodal baseline (config_004: pca_n2000+resnet50+avgpool+concat, acc=0.619) and an RNA-only baseline (config_029: pca_n2000+avgpool, acc=0.591), showing a ~2.8% accuracy gain from adding image. However, we lack an image-only baseline to decompose the contribution of each modality. config_039 (image_only, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool) is the cleanest complement: it shares the same image encoder (resnet50), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool) as the two completed experiments. This lets us isolate whether the image modality contributes independently or whether the multimodal gain is synergistic. Understanding this is critical before investing further experiments in more complex multimodal variants (different encoders, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion), as it tells us whether the image signal is a meaningful additive component or a minor correction. Under a limited budget, completing the modality decomposition (RNA-only, image-only, multimodal) with matched hyperparameters is the highest-information next step."
